{
  "round_analysis": {
    "summary": "Round 6 successfully executed its micro-optimization agenda. The SC min/max ablation conclusively shows SC min is the valuable extremum (cand62 F1=0.7453 vs cand61 F1=0.7393). The C0 log-energy coefficient candidate (cand64) achieved a new history best F1=0.7467 (+0.0028 vs history best) at a compact 161-dim. Extraction parameter changes (hop_length=256, n_fft=1024) both degraded performance vs the default settings, confirming the standard librosa frame parameters are near-optimal for this task. The optimization ceiling has not yet been reached, but gains remain small and within plausible CV noise.",

    "hypothesis_result": {
      "status": "partially_supported",
      "reason": "The SC ablation sub-hypothesis was well-tested and clearly answered: SC min carries the residual signal, not max. The hop_length sub-hypothesis was tested with good design fidelity but showed no improvement. The C0 exploratory sub-hypothesis was supported with a new history best. However, the overall framing of 'confirm the optimization ceiling' is contradicted by cand64 finding additional signal. Design fidelity is high across all five candidates — each tested exactly one controlled variation against the cand31 backbone."
    },

    "key_findings": [
      "Controlled SC extremum comparison: cand62 (SC 4-stat mean/std/median/min, 168-dim, F1=0.7453) vs cand61 (SC 4-stat mean/std/median/max, 168-dim, F1=0.7393) isolates SC min as +0.006 better than SC max under identical MFCC backbone. Mechanism hypothesis: SC min captures the valley-floor spectral contrast (minimum energy difference between peaks and valleys in each band), which may encode the flattened or exaggerated spectral envelope characteristic of sarcastic delivery more than peak contrast does.",
      "SC min subsumes SC max: cand62 (168-dim, F1=0.7453) slightly exceeds the full SC 5-stat cand31 (175-dim, F1=0.7438) while dropping SC max and using 7 fewer dimensions. This suggests SC max adds noise or redundancy when min is present, and the 5-stat SC configuration can be trimmed to 4-stat with min without loss.",
      "C0 log-energy coefficient adds genuine complementary signal: cand64 (MFCC C0-C20 6-stat no-skew + SC 5-stat, 161-dim, F1=0.7467) is the new history best at +0.0028 vs cand31 despite using 14 fewer dimensions and dropping skew aggregation. The C0 coefficient encodes per-frame log-energy, and its distributional statistics (particularly kurtosis of loudness over time) appear to capture emphasis patterns in sarcastic speech not represented by the spectral-shape coefficients C1-C20.",
      "Controlled extraction parameter comparison — hop_length: cand63 (hop=256, 175-dim, F1=0.7395) vs cand31 (hop=512, 175-dim, F1=0.7438) shows -0.0044 degradation. Doubling frame count did not yield more stable aggregation statistics; the additional temporal resolution either adds noise to higher-order statistics or subtly changes the spectral estimates due to increased frame overlap (75% overlap at hop=256/n_fft=2048 vs 75% at hop=512/n_fft=2048).",
      "Controlled extraction parameter comparison — n_fft: cand65 (n_fft=1024, 175-dim, F1=0.7307) vs cand31 (n_fft=2048, 175-dim, F1=0.7438) shows the largest degradation in this round at -0.0131. Halving the FFT window reduces frequency resolution, particularly harming lower MFCC coefficients and spectral contrast band separation. This confirms that the standard 93ms window provides sufficient temporal resolution while maintaining the frequency resolution needed for sarcasm-relevant spectral features."
    ],

    "positive_signals": [
      "cand64_c0_energy_coefficient: MFCC family (C0-C20, n_mfcc=21) with 6-stat aggregation (mean/std/min/max/median/kurtosis) at 126-dim + SC 5-stat at 35-dim = 161-dim total; F1=0.7467, +0.0028 vs history_best (cand31), +0.0453 vs baseline; mechanism: C0 log-energy distributional statistics (especially kurtosis) capture sarcastic loudness emphasis patterns absent from C1-C20 spectral-shape coefficients.",
      "cand62_sc_4stat_with_min: MFCC-20 7-stat (140-dim) + SC 4-stat mean/std/median/min (28-dim) = 168-dim; F1=0.7453, +0.0014 vs history_best, +0.0439 vs baseline; mechanism: SC valley-floor (min) encodes the minimum spectral peak-valley contrast per band, capturing moments of spectral flattening or exaggeration associated with sarcastic delivery."
    ],

    "negative_signals": [
      "cand65_shorter_fft_window: MFCC-20 7-stat + SC 5-stat with n_fft=1024 (175-dim); F1=0.7307, -0.0131 vs history_best; mechanism: halving FFT window degrades frequency resolution critical for low-order MFCC accuracy and spectral contrast band separation, outweighing any temporal resolution benefit.",
      "cand63_finer_hop_mfcc_sc: MFCC-20 7-stat + SC 5-stat with hop_length=256 (175-dim); F1=0.7395, -0.0044 vs history_best; mechanism: doubling frame count via finer hop does not improve aggregation statistic stability and may introduce noise from highly overlapping frames.",
      "cand61_sc_4stat_with_max: MFCC-20 7-stat + SC 4-stat mean/std/median/max (168-dim); F1=0.7393, -0.0045 vs history_best; SC max is the less informative extremum compared to SC min, contributing little beyond what mean/std/median already capture about spectral contrast distribution."
    ],

    "redundant_or_duplicate_strategies": [
      "cand61 and cand63 are not duplicates but are near-performance ties (F1=0.7393 vs 0.7395, delta=0.0002) despite testing completely different interventions (SC max-only vs finer hop). This coincidence should not be interpreted as the two modifications being equivalent — they happen to land at similar performance levels for unrelated reasons."
    ],

    "uncertainties": [
      "All deltas in this round (max spread ~0.016 between cand64 and cand65) are within plausible 5-fold CV noise on 690 samples. Without fold-level standard deviations, statistical significance of the cand64 improvement (+0.0028 vs history best) cannot be confirmed.",
      "cand64 changes two variables simultaneously vs cand31: it adds C0 but also drops skew aggregation and reduces from 7-stat to 6-stat on the MFCC side. The +0.0028 improvement cannot be cleanly attributed to C0 alone vs the dimension reduction from 175 to 161 (which may benefit the fixed gamma=0.0065 RBF kernel).",
      "C0 has very different scale from C1-C20 (log-energy vs cepstral coefficients). The improvement may depend critically on whether per-feature standardization is applied, and the result may not generalize if scaling changes.",
      "The fixed RBF SVM gamma=0.0065 interacts with dimensionality: cand64 at 161-dim may be in a slightly more favorable kernel geometry regime than cand31 at 175-dim, confounding the C0 signal attribution."
    ],

    "leads_from_this_round": [
      "C0 + SC min combination lead: cand64 (C0-C20, 6-stat, SC 5-stat, 161-dim, F1=0.7467) and cand62 (MFCC-20 7-stat, SC 4-stat with min, 168-dim, F1=0.7453) each independently exceed history best. Combining C0 inclusion with SC 4-stat-min aggregation (dropping SC max) could yield a more compact and potentially stronger configuration. Evidence: C0 and SC-min each contribute independent positive signal from different feature families.",
      "C0 isolation lead: cand64 confounds C0 addition with skew removal and dimension reduction. A controlled test of MFCC C0-C20 with full 7-stat aggregation + SC 5-stat (182-dim) vs cand31 (175-dim) would isolate C0's contribution, though the 182-dim may hit the dimensionality penalty zone identified in Round 3.",
      "SC min-only lead: Since cand62 (SC 4-stat with min) matched or exceeded the full SC 5-stat (cand31), and SC max appears inert, testing SC 3-stat (mean/std/min) — dropping median as well — could probe whether further SC compression is feasible, opening dimension budget for other additions like C0."
    ]
  }
}

{
  "round_analysis": {
    "summary": "Round 7 tested whether combining C0 inclusion and SC 4-stat-min aggregation would be additive, along with controlled variants for percentile aggregation, SC compression, skew re-inclusion, and mel-resolution change. The combination candidate cand71 achieved a new history best (F1=0.7524, +0.0057 vs history best), supporting the additivity hypothesis. Percentile aggregation (cand72) and reduced mel resolution (cand75) were clearly negative. SC 3-stat compression (cand73) essentially tied history best, confirming SC min carries most of the SC supplement value. Skew re-inclusion with C0 (cand74) was marginally positive vs history best but weaker than the skew-excluded cand71, reinforcing skew's dispensability.",

    "hypothesis_result": {
      "status": "partially_supported",
      "reason": "The core hypothesis—that C0 inclusion and SC 4-stat-min are additive—is supported: cand71 combined both and achieved +0.0057 vs history best (cand64). However, the secondary probes gave mixed results: percentile aggregation degraded performance rather than improving robustness, mel-resolution change was strongly negative, and the gain magnitude (+0.0057) remains within plausible 5-fold CV noise on 690 samples, so the additivity conclusion is tentative."
    },

    "key_findings": [
      "Controlled comparison—C0 6-stat + SC 4-stat-min (cand71, 154-dim, F1=0.7524) vs C0 6-stat + SC 5-stat (cand64/history best, 161-dim, F1=0.7467): dropping SC max and keeping SC min yields +0.0057. Since cand71 is also 7 dimensions smaller, the improvement may partly reflect tighter kernel geometry at 154-dim rather than pure SC-min superiority. The two effects are confounded.",
      "Controlled comparison—min/max vs Q10/Q90 in MFCC aggregation: cand72 (Q10/Q90, 161-dim, F1=0.7380) vs cand64 (min/max, 161-dim, F1=0.7467) at matched dimensionality shows -0.0087. Raw min/max carry more discriminative signal than robust percentiles for this task, suggesting sarcasm markers may reside in extreme frame values (e.g., sharp pitch/energy excursions) that percentile smoothing attenuates.",
      "Controlled comparison—SC aggregation depth: cand73 (SC 3-stat mean/std/min, 147-dim, F1=0.7466) vs cand71 (SC 4-stat mean/std/median/min, 154-dim, F1=0.7524) shows -0.0058 from dropping SC median. This is comparable to the R5 finding that SC 3-stat lost -0.0075 vs 5-stat (cand52 vs cand31), suggesting SC median carries genuine complementary information beyond mean/std/min.",
      "Controlled comparison—skew inclusion: cand74 (C0-C20 7-stat with skew + SC 4-stat-min, 175-dim, F1=0.7481) vs cand71 (C0-C20 6-stat no skew + SC 4-stat-min, 154-dim, F1=0.7524) shows -0.0043 from adding skew. This confounds the skew statistic itself with the 21-dim increase (175 vs 154), but consistently replicates the finding that skew is at best neutral and likely harmful through dimensionality bloat.",
      "Mel filterbank resolution: cand75 (n_mels=40, 161-dim, F1=0.7233) vs cand64 (n_mels=128 default, 161-dim, F1=0.7467) at matched dim shows -0.0234. The default 128 mel bands are substantially better, indicating higher MFCC coefficients (C10-C20) rely on fine spectral resolution for discriminative power; a coarser 40-band filterbank degrades their quality, likely washing out formant-level detail relevant to sarcastic vocal quality."
    ],

    "positive_signals": [
      "cand71 (C0-C20 6-stat no-skew + SC 4-stat mean/std/median/min): MFCC n_mfcc=21 with 6-stat aggregation (mean/std/min/max/median/kurtosis) concatenated with 7-band spectral_contrast 4-stat (mean/std/median/min), 154-dim total; F1=0.7524, +0.0057 vs history best, +0.0510 vs baseline; the two independently validated modifications appear additive, possibly because C0 captures utterance-level energy emphasis while SC-min captures timbral valley depth, providing complementary sarcasm cues that occupy orthogonal feature subspaces.",
      "cand74 (C0-C20 7-stat + SC 4-stat-min): MFCC n_mfcc=21 with 7-stat aggregation (including skew) + SC 4-stat, 175-dim; F1=0.7481, +0.0014 vs history best; marginal positive confirming C0 + SC-min combination value even with skew re-included, though weaker than cand71 due to skew/dimensionality overhead."
    ],

    "negative_signals": [
      "cand72 (C0-C20 percentile 6-stat + SC 5-stat): MFCC n_mfcc=21 with Q10/Q90 replacing min/max, 161-dim; F1=0.7380, -0.0087 vs history best; percentile smoothing removes extreme-frame information that likely encodes sarcastic prosodic exaggeration (sudden energy/pitch spikes).",
      "cand75 (C0-C20 6-stat n_mels=40 + SC 5-stat): MFCC n_mfcc=21 with n_mels=40 instead of default 128, 161-dim; F1=0.7233, -0.0234 vs history best; coarser mel filterbank severely degrades cepstral coefficient quality, particularly for higher-order MFCCs that capture fine spectral detail."
    ],

    "redundant_or_duplicate_strategies": [
      "cand73 (147-dim, F1=0.7466) is near-identical in outcome to cand64/history best (161-dim, F1=0.7467, delta=-0.0001). While they differ in SC aggregation (3-stat vs 5-stat), the indistinguishable metric outcome means cand73 provides no independent evidence beyond confirming SC median and max contribute minimally when SC min is already present. Should not be counted as an independent positive signal."
    ],

    "uncertainties": [
      "The new best cand71's +0.0057 vs history best is small relative to expected 5-fold CV variance on 690 samples; without fold-level standard deviations, statistical significance is unknown. This gain could be within noise.",
      "cand71 (154-dim) vs cand64 (161-dim) confounds the SC aggregation change with a 7-dim reduction; the fixed gamma=0.0065 RBF kernel behaves differently at different dimensionalities, so the improvement may partly reflect better kernel geometry rather than better feature content.",
      "cand74 vs cand71 confounds skew inclusion with a 21-dim increase (175 vs 154), making it impossible to isolate whether skew itself is harmful or dimensionality bloat is responsible for the -0.0043 drop.",
      "All candidates share identical audio loading (sr=22050), hop_length=512, n_fft=2048, and per-feature standardization assumptions; any systematic implementation difference (e.g., librosa version, edge-case short utterance handling) affects all results uniformly.",
      "The optimization trajectory is now 7 rounds deep with incremental gains converging; risk of overfitting to the specific 5-fold split structure increases with each round of selection."
    ],

    "leads_from_this_round": [
      "SC median isolation lead: cand71 (SC 4-stat with median+min, F1=0.7524) outperformed cand73 (SC 3-stat without median, F1=0.7466) by +0.0058, suggesting SC median carries signal. A controlled test of SC 5-stat (adding max back to cand71's configuration) at matched 154-dim (e.g., by slightly compressing MFCC aggregation) could clarify whether SC max was genuinely harmful or merely added unhelpful dimensions.",
      "Dimensionality-controlled C0 validation lead: cand71 achieved best at 154-dim, below the 161-175 range of prior bests. Testing the cand71 feature set at exactly 161-dim (e.g., adding one more SC statistic or one additional aggregation stat) would help disentangle feature-content improvement from kernel-geometry improvement at gamma=0.0065.",
      "Extremum preservation lead: cand72's failure with Q10/Q90 vs min/max (-0.0087) suggests frame-level extremes carry sarcasm signal. Exploring additional extreme-sensitive statistics (e.g., range=max-min, IQR, peak-to-mean ratio) as supplementary features to the cand71 backbone could capture excursion magnitude directly.",
      "Plateau detection lead: Seven rounds have brought F1 from 0.7013 (baseline) to 0.7524 (cand71), with the last three rounds producing diminishing gains (+0.0028, +0.0057). The optimization may be approaching the ceiling for MFCC+SC features under fixed RBF SVM with gamma=0.0065; investigating whether gamma tuning or a fundamentally different feature family (e.g., pre-trained audio embeddings) would break the plateau could be informative, though model changes are out of scope for feature extraction."
    ]
  }
}
